**No.** KCNH4 (Q9UQ05) is 814 aa; SMOC1 (Q9H4F8, isoform 1) is 434 aa. Twice SMOC1 would be 868 aa, so KCNH4 is only ~1.88× as long.

Checks: KCNH4's stated length 814 is corroborated by its sequence features (the natural variant G→R at position 797 indeed falls on a Gly in the C-terminal "…SASPHG⁷⁹⁷PPRCSAAWKPPQLLIPP"), and both molecular weights (~89.9 kDa / ~48.2 kDa) match their residue counts at ~110 Da/residue.

